# Badger Phase 3 Engineering Rules

Badger is an AI-native developer networking platform.

Current Status

Phase 1
Tunnel Engine
Production Ready

Phase 2
Developer Observability
Production Ready

Phase 3
Multi-tenant SaaS Platform
Currently in development

────────────────────────────────────

Mission

Build a SaaS platform around the existing tunnel engine.

The tunnel engine is considered stable.

The observability pipeline is considered stable.

Never redesign either subsystem.

Only extend them.

────────────────────────────────────

Core Principles

Workspace is the primary domain model.

Every authenticated user automatically owns one Personal Workspace.

Shared workspaces are optional.

Organizations do not exist as a first-class entity.

Workspaces support:

• Personal developers
• Freelancers
• Teams
• Enterprises

Never create architecture that only works for organizations.

────────────────────────────────────

Architecture

Dashboard

↓

NestJS API

↓

Repositories

↓

Supabase

Never bypass the API.

Never query Supabase directly from React.

Never couple business logic to Supabase SDK.

Supabase is an infrastructure dependency.

Business logic must remain database agnostic.

────────────────────────────────────

Authentication

Supabase Auth

JWT

Bearer Tokens

Stateless

No server-side sessions.

CLI authentication must use OAuth browser flow.

Never ask users to manually paste JWTs.

────────────────────────────────────

Code Quality

Strict TypeScript

No any

No placeholder implementations

No TODO comments

No mocked production logic

No duplicated code

Keep files reasonably small

Prefer dependency injection

Prefer interfaces

Prefer composition

────────────────────────────────────

Database

Every migration must be additive.

Never remove production columns.

Never rename production columns.

Never perform destructive migrations.

Every table must include:

id

created_at

updated_at

Indexes

Foreign Keys

Use UUID primary keys.

────────────────────────────────────

Security

Never trust workspace IDs from clients.

Resolve workspace membership server-side.

Validate every JWT.

Every endpoint must verify authorization.

Every websocket must authenticate before tunnel creation.

────────────────────────────────────

Compatibility

Do not break:

Tunnel Protocol

CLI Commands

Inspector

Replay

Dashboard

Public APIs

────────────────────────────────────

Testing

Every phase must:

Compile

Pass lint

Pass tests

Maintain backward compatibility

Have no regressions

────────────────────────────────────

Output

Implement only the requested phase.

Do not anticipate future phases.

Avoid unnecessary refactoring.

Keep commits focused.

Document architectural decisions.
